      content: '**Expense Tracker** – a personal finance app.\n\nUser stories:\n1. As a user I can add an expense (title, amount, category, date, note) with validation.\n2. I can see all expenses, filter by category and month, search by title, and sort by date/amount.\n3. I can edit or delete an expense (with confirmation).\n4. The dashboard shows total this month, total by category (bar chart made of divs), and the 5 latest expenses.\n5. A monthly budget can be set; the dashboard warns when spending exceeds 80% / 100%.\n6. Data survives refresh (localStorage). Theme (light/dark) is remembered.\n7. Leaving the form with unsaved changes asks for confirmation.\n\nNon-functional: responsive, accessible labels and focus, lazy-loaded pages, unit tests for the store, deploy on Netlify/Vercel.',
